WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.331
- Look at your cute little jean number.

00:00:02.331 --> 00:00:05.130
Okay so you like to dance on camera too.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.040
She's known for dancing,

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.960
but I just wanted to show you

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:08.830
you've got competition.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.210
We have a really awesome video

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.984
of Nikolaj and his dance moves.

00:00:11.984 --> 00:00:14.567
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:25.564
(audience applauding)

00:00:25.564 --> 00:00:26.397
- It is now.

00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:27.230
- Be proud.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.063
Be proud of it.

00:00:28.063 --> 00:00:28.896
- I just have one question.

00:00:28.896 --> 00:00:30.940
How much cake did you eat

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.930
of someone else's before
doing this video? (laughing)

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.230
- A lot, a lot.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.120
- You were on something.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.167
- I should say that my wife was doing this

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.043
dancing show back home,

00:00:39.043 --> 00:00:40.860
so I was trying to inspire her that's why.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.230
- You inspired me so well done.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.047
I love it it's awesome.

00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:45.880
(audience applauding)

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.360
So, your new show is about

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.980
you going home to Louisiana, right?

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.070
So was that a weird thing?

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.610
'Cause it's been a couple years, right?

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:55.720
- Yeah it was two years before
I had went back for the show.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:56.580
So really long time.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.230
It was like right when I moved out here

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.740
I hadn't gone back since, so.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.573
- Yeah.

00:01:00.573 --> 00:01:01.406
That's super cool.

00:01:01.406 --> 00:01:04.040
So did you get to celebrate
Mardi Gras back home?

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:04.934
Did you...

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:06.550
'Cause now you're 21 right so-

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:07.520
- I know I'm 21.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.673
- You can enjoy Mardi Gras properly.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.050
- No, I haven't been back for Mardi Gras.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.180
My mom is there right now

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:14.480
and she was like sending me pictures

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:15.820
and videos of my brothers,

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.940
hanging on the fences and beads.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.090
And there's thongs

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:20.490
and bras everywhere,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.080
the whole thing.
- Just to explain Denmark,

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.480
have you ever been to Mardi Gras?

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.970
- I was there just after

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:27.950
and I saw beads hanging from every tree.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:28.783
I did not understand anything.

00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:30.334
- Then you missed the show.

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:31.167
(laughing)

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.160
Yes, it's quite a show.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:32.993
- It's crazy.

00:01:32.993 --> 00:01:34.590
- It's quite an experience if you ever go.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:35.960
I've been once.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:36.793
- Really?

00:01:36.793 --> 00:01:37.725
- Yes.

00:01:37.725 --> 00:01:38.558
And it's...

00:01:38.558 --> 00:01:39.391
Yeah I was like,

00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:40.367
"I don't have any beats ma'am,

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.397
"but nice job God."

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.480
What was your first visit like?

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:47.313
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:47.313 --> 00:01:48.480
My first time in Mardi Gras?

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.313
- Yeah.

00:01:49.313 --> 00:01:50.146
- So crazy.

00:01:50.146 --> 00:01:51.360
I remember, like I said,

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.150
bras, panties,

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.930
people shirtless on floats,

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.250
that's the normal thing in Mardi Gras.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.920
So it's really crazy.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:01:59.753
There's like...

00:01:59.753 --> 00:02:00.650
I mean, now that I'm 21,

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:02.160
I feel like it'd be even more fun,

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.140
but really crazy.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.020
And just so spirited I don't know.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.340
Everyone's like family
back home in Louisiana.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.880
So everyone's just all there to have

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.760
a good time catch beads,

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:13.610
kind of unsanitary

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.780
now I think about it, but yeah.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.130
- The COVID police would frown.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.099
- Right.

00:02:18.099 --> 00:02:19.940
The COVID police would hate us.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.070
- Well, let's talk about the new series.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:22.360
So it's called "Addison Rae Goes Home."

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.880
So is that pretty much what happens,

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.400
everybody just tracks that journey?

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.520
- So I don't go home.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.353
No, I'm kidding.

00:02:27.353 --> 00:02:29.340
- Oh God. (indistinct)

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.930
- Okay so yeah, I go back to Louisiana,

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.600
go back to where I was born

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.660
and raised and just get to
reconnect with everybody.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.650
Do a lot of things that I even didn't do

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:40.570
when I lived back home,

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:41.740
which was like craw fishing.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.960
I go craw fishing in the show.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.520
- Oh, all the things that people do-

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.020
- Right, kind of like...

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:46.853
You know when people are like,

00:02:46.853 --> 00:02:48.147
"Oh you live in Texas,

00:02:48.147 --> 00:02:50.127
"do you ride a donkey to school?

00:02:50.127 --> 00:02:51.533
"Or a horse?"
- They'd always be like,

00:02:51.533 --> 00:02:52.628
"Did you ride a horse to school?"

00:02:52.628 --> 00:02:54.247
I'm like, "What?

00:02:54.247 --> 00:02:55.200
"Yeah no."

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.350
- Me riding an alligator to class, no.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:58.710
- We took a Honda Accord.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.630
So, I was like, "No."

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:01.463
Yeah.
- Right.

00:03:01.463 --> 00:03:03.357
I'm like, "No, we got there safely

00:03:03.357 --> 00:03:04.190
"and normally."

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:05.820
But yeah, just kind of doing things

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.580
that are basic Louisiana things,

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.730
and then doing them with my family,

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:10.563
which is really fun.

00:03:10.563 --> 00:03:11.396
- That's awesome.

00:03:11.396 --> 00:03:13.430
- Well, what was the hardest
thing to share about yourself?

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:16.083
'Cause you have a few followers.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.930
'Cause it's hard sometimes
for me over 20 years

00:03:21.803 --> 00:03:22.636
'cause I'm unfiltered

00:03:22.636 --> 00:03:23.527
but there are certain
things that I'm like,

00:03:23.527 --> 00:03:24.830
"Ooh maybe I'll keep that for myself."

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.237
Has there been anything that you're like,

00:03:26.237 --> 00:03:27.940
"Ugh, that was hard to share."?

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.320
- Yeah, in the show,

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.360
which I hate crying in front of people,

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.200
but I do it anyways.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.573
'Cause I'm a big cry baby.

00:03:34.573 --> 00:03:35.406
- Me too.

00:03:35.406 --> 00:03:36.239
- But I definitely hate it.

00:03:36.239 --> 00:03:37.090
Like I feel...

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:37.923
I don't know.

00:03:37.923 --> 00:03:39.310
I just hate feeling like...

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:40.863
I feel guilty for some reason when I cry.

00:03:40.863 --> 00:03:43.602
Like, Oh, "Oh I don't
want to guilt people."

00:03:43.602 --> 00:03:44.435
It feels great.

00:03:44.435 --> 00:03:45.690
Don't get me wrong.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.523
- It's a nice release.

00:03:46.523 --> 00:03:47.770
- But I feel like it's...

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:48.603
I don't know.

00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:49.710
I guess it puts a lot on people

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:50.543
to watch someone cry.

00:03:50.543 --> 00:03:51.376
'Cause you're also like,

00:03:51.376 --> 00:03:52.209
"What do you do in this situation

00:03:52.209 --> 00:03:53.042
"when someone cries?"

00:03:53.042 --> 00:03:55.840
But I really opened up just kind of about

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:56.673
my mental health

00:03:56.673 --> 00:03:57.506
and like things that,

00:03:57.506 --> 00:03:58.890
which I feel like that's so cliche.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:03:59.723
'Cause everyone's always like,

00:03:59.723 --> 00:04:00.940
"Oh you know..."

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:01.773
It's hard but it's true.

00:04:01.773 --> 00:04:03.030
'Cause it's like a really big thing.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:06.506
And I think maybe not even for me,

00:04:06.506 --> 00:04:07.750
but for a lot of people

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.567
it's hard to confront those feelings of,

00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:11.630
the way you feel about yourself

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:13.240
from a public perception

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.827
and seeing, "Oh, maybe I am that way

00:04:15.827 --> 00:04:16.917
"that people say that I am.

00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:18.157
"And maybe I don't know,

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.567
"maybe I do not look great in anything

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:21.400
"and whatever."

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.332
You kind of start-

00:04:22.332 --> 00:04:23.490
- You can get lost in all
that conversation though.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.950
Especially being young in the industry,

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.040
I do feel like people start saying things

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:27.920
and they project on you

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.230
and then you get lost.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:30.247
And you're like, "I'm not that way.

00:04:30.247 --> 00:04:31.350
"Am I that way or am I..."

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.650
You just start questioning.
- Questioning.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:33.483
- Yeah.

00:04:33.483 --> 00:04:34.316
Does it ever annoy you

00:04:34.316 --> 00:04:35.490
when people talk about
you in the public eye

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.090
and they have no idea what
they're talking about?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.103
- Yeah.

00:04:39.103 --> 00:04:40.690
(laughing)

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:41.730
- You're like, "I don't care."

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.167
- He's just like, "One, I don't care,

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:44.800
"and two you guys just saw
the dancing video of me.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:45.837
So what (indistinct).

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.195
- I have set the bar.

00:04:48.195 --> 00:04:49.028
- Right.

